.venv
__pycache__
.pytest_cache

# v1's PDF capture (archive/Initial_EO_Research/eo_pdf_capture/EO_PDFs/) was 143
# PDFs, ~33 MB, matched by this rule and therefore never tracked -- a fresh clone
# never had it. It was deleted locally on 2026-09-04 during cleanup. Nothing is
# lost: the post-mortem evidence is the tracked code and CSVs beside it
# (get_eo.py, URLs.txt, eo_summary.csv, extract.txt), and the capture is
# reproducible from those if it is ever wanted again.
*.pdf

# The working store stays local: eo.db holds every run and every raw model
# response. The two published artefacts are the analysis database and the
# flat-file export -- both derived from public Federal Register data, both
# rebuildable with `eo analysis-db` / `eo export`.
#
# data/raw/ was the re-fetchable source-text cache (1,556 .txt files, 18 MB).
# Deleted locally on 2026-09-04: it was byte-identical to documents.body_text in
# eo.db, so it duplicated data already held twice over. `eo fetch` simply
# recreates it -- ~1,556 requests at a 0.2s pause, roughly 10 minutes and no
# model cost -- and it can also be reconstructed offline from eo.db.
data/*
!data/analysis.db
!data/export/

.env
my_secrets.py
.DS_Store
